# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env  --  the ONLY two variables the browser bundle may ever see.
#
# The publishable key is public by design: it ships inside the JavaScript
# bundle and anyone can read it. Nothing in this application may rely on it
# being secret. All security rests on RLS policies and the authorization checks
# inside the SECURITY DEFINER functions in
# supabase/migrations/0006_functions.sql.
#
# `sb_publishable_…` is Supabase's replacement for the legacy `anon` JWT. It
# resolves to the same `anon` Postgres role, so every policy written against
# `anon` applies to it unchanged. Either format works; the dashboard hands you
# this one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.seed  --  NOT this file. Create it separately; it is gitignored.
#
# The secret key (`sb_secret_…`, formerly service_role) bypasses RLS
# completely. It is used by `npm run db:seed` and nothing else. It must never
# appear in src/, never carry a VITE_ prefix (that would inline it into the
# bundle), and never be committed.
#
#   SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_your-key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
